        <h1 class="article_headline"> Lamine Yamal sets new record as youngest player to feature at a UEFA European Championship</h1>
        <p class="article_info">
            <span class="article_date">Sunday, July 14, 2024</span>
        </p>
      </header>




        <div class="article_summary">
          <h2 class="hidden">Article summary</h2>
          <div>
            <p><p>Spain's Lamine Yamal shattered the record for youngest EURO player after making his debut against Croatia. Meet the prodigious talents who have marked the competition. </p></p>
          </div>
        </div>






        <div class="article_content d3-plugin" data-plugin="quote-author">
          <h2 class="hidden">Article body</h2>
          <div class="article_body">
            <div class="article-embedded_image embedded-image-free"><figure class="article_picture" data-path="https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg" data-id="028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000" data-credits="" ><div class="pflazyload-wrapper pflazyload-wrapper-free">
<picture>
<source media="(min-width: 0px)"  srcset="https://img.uefa.com/imgml/void.svg" data-srcset="https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=158 158w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=276 276w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=280 280w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=369 369w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=490 490w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=556 556w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=656 656w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=988 988w, https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=2048 2048w" data-format="f1" ><img alt="" title="" data-sizes="auto" loading="lazy"  src="https://img.uefa.com/imgml/void.svg" data-src="https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028e-1b239adf9c20-87ee02c157a1-1000/format/free1/yamal.jpeg?imwidth=158" width="1080" height="1350" data-format="f1" data-fallback="" class="pflazyload lazyfade picture article--img img-responsive" >
</picture>
</div>
</figure></div><p>Spain winger Lamine Yamal smashed the record for youngest player to have featured at a UEFA EURO finals after taking to the field aged only 16 years 338 days <a href="https://www.uefa.com/euro2024/match/2036163--spain-vs-croatia/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self">against Croatia at EURO 2024</a>.</p><p>The Barcelona prodigy beat the benchmark set by Poland's Kacper KozÅowski, who made his competition debut at EURO 2020 at the age of just 17 years 246 days. </p><h2><strong>Youngest player to appear</strong></h2><p><strong>Lamine Yamal (16 years 338 days)<br/></strong>The Spain ace was long tipped to take the record and duly earned his place in the history books when he started against Croatia at the Olympiastadion in Berlin. Not only did he quickly impress, he set up Dani Carvajal's goal in a 3-0 victory, naturally also making him the youngest player to serve up an assist in a EURO finals game.</p><p><b>EURO's youngest players<br/></b>16 years 338 days: Lamine Yamal (<a href="https://www.uefa.com/euro2024/match/2036163--spain-vs-croatia/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self"><b>Spain</b> 3-0 Croatia</a>, 15/06/2024)<br/>17 yrs 246 days: Kacper KozÅowski (<a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/2024463--spain-vs-poland/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self">Spain 1-1 </a><b><a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/2024463--spain-vs-poland/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self">Poland</a></b>, 19/06/2021)<br/>17 yrs 349 days: Jude Bellingham (<b><a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/2024451--england-vs-croatia/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self">England</a></b><a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/2024451--england-vs-croatia/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self"> 1-0 Croatia</a>, 13/06/2021)<br/>18 yrs 71 days: Jetro Willems (<b><a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/2003321--netherlands-vs-denmark/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self">Netherlands</a></b><a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/2003321--netherlands-vs-denmark/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self"> 0-1 Denmark</a>, 09/06/2012)<br/>18 yrs 115 days: Enzo Scifo (<b><a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/3450--belgium-vs-yugoslavia/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self">Belgium</a></b><a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/3450--belgium-vs-yugoslavia/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self"> 2-0 Yugoslavia</a>, 13/06/1984)</p><h2><strong>Youngest goalkeeper to appear</strong></h2><p><strong>JosÃ©Â Ãngel Iribar (21 years 108 days)</strong><br/>Younger goalkeepers have been included in EURO squadsÂ â Iker Casillas at UEFA EURO 2000 and Igor Akinfeev at UEFA EURO 2004 â but Iribar made the mark as the youngest keeper during <a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/3993--spain-vs-hungary/" notaddlevel="true" target="_self">Spain's 2-1 win against Hungary</a> on 17 June 1964. Four days later he was also EURO's youngest winning goalkeeper as his team beat the USSR 2-1.</p><h2><strong>Youngest player to score</strong></h2><p><strong>Lamine Yamal (16 years 362 days)</strong><br/>Just over three weeks after becoming the youngest player to appear in a EURO, the teenage winger took the scoring record as well with a sensational equaliser in <a href="https://www.uefa.com/euro2024/match/2036209--spain-vs-france/" notaddlevel="true" target="_blank">Spain's semi-final against France</a>. Yamal eclipsed the longstanding mark of Johan Vonlanthen, who was aged 18 years 141 days when he struck at EURO 2004, <a href="https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/match/73916--switzerland-vs-france/" notaddlevel="true" target="_blank">also against France</a>, four days after Wayne Rooney had become the youngest scorer in EURO history with two goals against Vonlanthen's Switzerland side.</p><div class="article-embedded_video pull-left embedded-image-single embedded-image-big d3-plugin" data-plugin="videoavailability" data-options="{&quot;videoIds&quot;:[&quot;028f-1b54485266d3-72b8c20252fc-1000&quot;]}" >

